          "name": "search_notes",
          "response": {
            "output": "[guitar-pedalboard.md]\n# Guitar Pedalboard\n\nThe board lives in the den, next to the record shelves. Signal chain,\nin order from the guitar: tuner, compressor, overdrive, fuzz,\nmodulation (chorus), delay, reverb, then into the amp. Fuzz goes after\noverdrive and before modulation deliberately, putting fuzz any later\nin the chain makes it sound thin and buzzy instead of thick.\n\nPower comes from a single isolated-output supply, not a daisy chain,\nafter a daisy-chained delay pedal picked up an audible hum from a\ndigital pedal sharing its power line. Cables get an ohms check with a\nmultimeter every few months; a bad cable is still the most common\nreason a \"dead\" signal chain turns out to have nothing wrong with any\nof the pedals themselves.\n"
          }
        },
